TELOMERE-CCC2-1:{"chunk":"c07","format":"ccc2-wire/1","records":[{"buys":"the fast prime counter was the facet recursion all along — the D2 identification","checksum":"e0aadd1336575f9313020c64966bc1afacc966ea14b1155cd73abebb5a0851c8","id":"B1","limits":"same computation, new language; no new algorithm","type":"B","x":"Lehmer's phi-recursion","y":"the link recursion on the divisor complex"},{"buys":"iterated to all orders the split is the D1 face-sum — 'the sieve was doing splits before we knew her name for them'","checksum":"133bdd5440757e1a42c24fb92c498d1f3f9478d223220369b696f3c547a13032","id":"B2","limits":"a conceptual identification; the numerics rest on D1/D2","type":"B","x":"territory removal in the sieve","y":"her soft-limit/splitting move (arXiv:2405.09608)"},{"buys":"forces zeta(1+it) != 0 — the Weil-shaped mechanism in miniature, with the contradiction visible in a way the trig identity hides","checksum":"53131bbd3d5fe937786b41f62d8af3dd6bef205aea74d5ab71f71a3c5c4d7f6e","id":"B3","limits":"the analytic singularity structure (residue -m) is housed by the complex, not derived","type":"B","x":"3-4-1 positivity (3+4cos(theta)+cos(2theta) >= 0 on -zeta'/zeta)","y":"nonnegative stratum energies e_{p,k} >= 0 termwise"},{"checksum":"68ea2042cdbeb38328dd9c4d6b28cef43532b1a9cad33cad51846b3bb5e33cf9","id":"C1","kind":"claim","label":"never put the answer in by hand — the sieve never tests primality with a predicate","note":"deepest applied generative insight of the Figueiredo transfer (user's standing steer, nodes 1/5); applied throughout the program","status":"heuristic","type":"C"},{"checksum":"44a357073414303b4536726a9b341949d0c107da452995ade6fb7afc46fd1181","id":"C2","kind":"question","label":"Does this arc belong in a paper, and which one? (node 7)","note":"NOT the primorial-wheel paper (different subject: wheel state-space reduction mod 210). This arc wants its own expository/synthesis paper — 'a geometric language for sieve theory' — not a claimed breakthrough (D6's framing appears new; the underlying computations are classical). Outline drafted 2026-09-30 (PAPER_OUTLINE.md, updated to cover D10/Node 11/CCM/Nodes 13-14 + failures appendix). Awaiting user approval on title/scope + prior-art search before novelty claims.","status":"unstated","type":"C"},{"checksum":"c33e4d0e1861ffc2560a0a0dddf52cf5168f75e8fad25cabb43820999171ebb8","conventions":["D-item numbering here is the tree's own (D1–D8); the wire ids are D1–D8 of this chunk."],"generates":[{"prescription":"vertices = primes <= N; faces = prime sets with product <= N (the divisor complex), as in sieve_complex.py","stage":"build complex"},{"prescription":"assign Mobius weights to faces per the companion DERIVATIONS.md","stage":"weight faces"},{"prescription":"sum the signed face weights — the total is the Chebyshev psi(x) observable","stage":"read observable"}],"honest_boundary":"The text marks this 'verified' but gives no recomputation steps here; the full derivation lives in the companion DERIVATIONS.md — do not present as a new theorem. Honest label per the text: 'classical theorems in new clothes'.","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D1","rule":"psi(x) = sum over faces S of w(S) (signed face-sum; Mobius inversion reframed on the divisor complex)","subtitle":"Chebyshev psi(x) as a signed face-sum (Mobius, reframed)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"corrected sieve equals the classical primes","expected":"match"},{"check":"link recursion exact","expected":"exact"}]},{"checksum":"b1825627b7269105b5d5023b7a65e56551252df7cc173d795bd5420e1b8f994d","generates":[{"prescription":"recurse on the link of the vertex: count with p_a forbidden minus with p_a divided out","stage":"remove prime p_a"},{"prescription":"apply the recursion to all orders — the link recursion is the face-recursion of the complex","stage":"iterate"}],"honest_boundary":"a mechanism identity only; it does not by itself speed prime counting beyond Lehmer's known algorithm","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D2","rule":"phi(x,a) = phi(x,a-1) - phi(x/p_a,a-1)","subtitle":"Lehmer's phi-recursion IS the link recursion","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"recursion-vs-link analogue","expected":"verified"}]},{"checksum":"84fe665df014c601365e101fd782046ce991ee1c81fc5ba4e7075eaea43308e0","generates":[{"prescription":"for each prime p, form dist(n, pZ)","stage":"distance functions"},{"prescription":"multiply over primes up to the cutoff — the product vanishes exactly at composites","stage":"product"},{"prescription":"the points where F does not vanish are the primes","stage":"read support"}],"honest_boundary":"a restatement of the sieve's marking rule, not a primality test — the sieve never tests primality with a predicate","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D3","rule":"F(n) = prod dist(n, pZ); composites = zero locus of F, primes = its support","subtitle":"Binary/zero-locus form of primality","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"zero-locus analogue","expected":"verified"}]},{"checksum":"c8471e26938e35756ce2763f2e2d6a59359451a1cde7a40471096e550c9d712c","generates":[{"prescription":"weight each face by the signed log-product over the product","stage":"assign weights"},{"prescription":"sum over all faces — the limit is the Prime Number Theorem: 'the weighted infinite simplex has total weight 1'","stage":"sum"},{"prescription":"verify that the weights' Dirichlet generating function is -zeta'/zeta^2","stage":"generating function"}],"honest_boundary":"the weights are SIGNED (alternating) — no positive region found; this derives the PNT framing, not a positivity source. Sharpest open question at this node: a positive region with these weights as stratum residues?","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D4","rule":"w(S) = (-1)^{|S|+1} log(prod S) / prod S; sum_S w(S) -> 1","subtitle":"Canonical face-weights; the PNT as total weight 1","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"partial sum at 2*10^6","expected":"1.001658"},{"check":"generating function matches -zeta'/zeta^2","expected":"~4 digits"}]},{"checksum":"89ddd63b18a341603fe97eb55529795f7f5d1c1c64536b91ad72c7314022cb60","generates":[{"prescription":"removing one generator splits the count into two terms (the soft-limit/splitting move, cf. arXiv:2405.09608)","stage":"identify the move"},{"prescription":"apply the split to all orders — the iterated expansion is the D1 face-sum","stage":"iterate"}],"honest_boundary":"a conceptual identification (D2 numerics cover it), not a new theorem","honest_label":"conjectural","id":"D5","rule":"phi(x,a) = phi(x,a-1) - phi(x/p_a,a-1) iterated to all orders = the D1 face-sum","subtitle":"Territory removal as the soft-limit/splitting move","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"numerical coverage of the identification","criterion":"identification is conceptual in the text; numerical coverage deferred to D1/D2","pending":true}]},{"checksum":"19caa4e838cf718929dac76dee632e76b41cbed1f49581c8ae7e343e6a7ffc61","generates":[{"prescription":"replace the residue marking by R_p — this SEPARATES markers (primes) from survivors (twin-prime lowers)","stage":"deform the marking rule"},{"prescription":"check the exact deformed mu-identity at the static z-sieve (z=30, x=200000)","stage":"static z-sieve mu-identity"},{"prescription":"take the renormalized total weight limit S(z) -> 2C_2","stage":"renormalize"}],"honest_boundary":"pi_2(x) ~ Sx/(log x)^2 remains the UNPROVEN twin conjecture (ratio 1.6091 at 2*10^5) — we verify the algebra, not the conjecture","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D6","rule":"R_p = {0} (p=2), {0,-2} (p odd); face multiplicities m(S) = prod|R_p|; delta(z) = prod(1-|R_p|/p); S(z) -> 2C_2 = 1.32032","subtitle":"Hardy-Littlewood twin constant as renormalized total weight","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"generative survivors <= 200000","expected":"exactly the 2160 twin lowers"},{"check":"S(x,z)/x -> delta(z)","expected":"6 digits at z=7"},{"check":"S(100)","expected":"1.3228, against 1.32032"}]},{"checksum":"6d25b8d97aae4356eb340435d6b01fde9fdbddd5396ecbe126d696c246341e76","generates":[{"prescription":"the von Mangoldt-weighted Dirichlet series, log zeta, and the Mertens product are positive objects — locate them first","stage":"locate the primitives"},{"prescription":"the weight generating function factors as (positive) * (sum mu(m)m^{-s}) — the signs enter only through the Mobius inclusion-exclusion factor","stage":"factor the signs"},{"prescription":"delta(X) > 0 monotone -> 0 while sum_{d<=X} mu(d)/d oscillates in sign toward the same 0","stage":"compare the two limits"}],"honest_boundary":"concludes the signs are an expansion artifact, not a property of the volume — a location claim, not a construction of the positive region itself","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D7","rule":"-zeta'/zeta = sum Lambda(n)n^{-s} (Lambda >= 0); log zeta(s) > 0; delta(z) = prod(1-1/p) > 0; -log delta(z) a manifestly positive prime sum","subtitle":"Where positivity lives (9a)","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"manifestly positive prime sum","expected":"6 digits"},{"check":"classical 3-4-1 template re-verified from the Lambda-sieve","expected":"sum stays positive, grows 2.26 -> 8.30 -> 20.62 as sigma -> 1+"}]},{"checksum":"1e86df03690407ddd0eefbd6c496a6ee2b82eda1e49bea28ba40f8fb65831cd8","generates":[{"prescription":"write -zeta'/zeta as vertex-tower energies E0/E1/E2","stage":"restate the series"},{"prescription":"3+4cos(theta)+cos(2theta) as (1/2)|1+e^{i theta}|^4 — an |Q|^2 form","stage":"restate the polynomial"},{"prescription":"a zero on Re(s)=1 would force negative-infinite total energy from nonnegative strata — impossible","stage":"run the contradiction"}],"honest_boundary":"the singularity structure (residue -m) is analytic fact the complex houses but does NOT derive — same traffic, new bridge, no new theorem yet","honest_label":"computationally_verified","id":"D8","rule":"-zeta'/zeta as vertex-tower energies E0/E1/E2; trig polynomial = (1/2)|1+e^{i theta}|^4; stratum energies e_{p,k} >= 0 termwise","subtitle":"The full 3-4-1 argument in the sieve's energy language","type":"D","verified":[{"check":"stratum identity","expected":"6 digits"}]},{"checksum":"d2539b7419c4d2ea6c125f65a457b5b918bab812ae6fd2d63da110aa3370c922","id":"G1","result":"no positive region, no canonical form found; everything depends on the cutoff N","title":"Naive finite incidence complex (node 2)","transfer":"killed the naive hope; forced node 4 (the N->infinity limit question)","tried":"sieve_complex.py: vertices = primes <= N, faces = prime sets with product <= N (the divisor complex); Betti numbers grow with N (N=1000: [74,101,26,0]); corrected sieve equals the classical primes; link recursion exact","type":"G","verdict":"CLOSED negative — no positive region, no canonical form; everything cutoff-N-dependent."},{"checksum":"fdda9961aa23258eddd366016b331aea33fca7ad6f0e1054df1ed442d95e3d21","id":"G2","result":"(i) the D8 deformation seed is killed: 3-4-1 transports to zeta_R (verified) but zeta_R is an Euler product, hence zero-free for Re(s)>1 — the machine runs with nothing to exclude; the pole merely gets heavier (order 2, verified). (ii) Positivity is blind left of the line: Dirichlet-series positivity converges only for sigma>1; the crossing is done by analytic input (partial fractions, zeta'/zeta bounds) — geometry owns positivity, analysis owns continuation. (iii) Parity barrier: pure sieve positivity cannot resolve omega(n) parity (Selberg) — analytic input is necessary. (iv) Literature: trig-polynomial optimization is saturated (Mossinghoff-Trudgian-Yang 2022: R=5.558691, 'near its intrinsic limit'; Bellotti-Trudgian-Yang 2026: 1/(4.896 log|t|)).","title":"Sieve-positivity route to RH via the 3-4-1 deformation (9c)","transfer":"RH needs analytic-continuation input; geometry owns positivity, analysis owns continuation","tried":"transport the 3-4-1 deformation seed to zeta_R","type":"G","verdict":"CLOSED NEGATIVE by theorem, not by difficulty."},{"checksum":"d61216eba0018943f2361638f37c13193b261b470805d81216b4ba1a233dc040","id":"G3","result":"all 32 real Fejer-Riesz factors c=(c_k) are FULLY DENSE — 17/17 nonzero at 1e-6 relative tolerance (sparsest at 1e-3 still 15/17); a_k lags 14/17 nonzero; participation ratio 3.62; coefficients span 3 orders of magnitude with mass piled at high lags (c11..c16); the density holds across EVERY zero-reflection choice, so it is structural, not an annealing accident; Table-5 internal consistency verified to 5e-15; F16>=0 on fine grid (zero_free_support.py)","title":"Saturated degree-16 optimizers have no small-support structure (9c')","transfer":"the sieve's small-support |Q|^2 language captures 3-4-1 (9b) but not the saturated optimum — the remaining slack is genuinely numerical, not geometric. Consistent with 9c's 'near intrinsic limit'.","tried":"F16 (Mossinghoff-Trudgian 2015, Table 5 — the degree-16 optimizer behind R0<5.57353; MTY 2022's 'essentially saturated' method)","type":"G","verdict":"CLOSED NEGATIVE — saturation comes from numerical optimization over R^16, not from a hidden small charge pattern."},{"checksum":"807ac2528c4d0c6d714d076b19b3b1824704b80603231f723c6a96b2a90f72da","from":"D7","id":"L1","rel":"supports","to":"D8","type":"L"},{"checksum":"e0e68838d822bad23991b63f6a4122ab5b19923480c0d72292e9d51af6490c25","from":"G2","id":"L2","rel":"bounds","to":"V4","type":"L"},{"checksum":"542cdbbd47cd3b66b99cdd7d30bb84b134b43be733c5bcda1a6ad64de4e2fba3","consequence":"the program this tree records is pursued: the sieve is a deterministic relational machine ('composites relating to the primes and the primes relating back to zero'); her binary/geometric work is the same kind of move — definition through relations, not intrinsic coordinates","id":"V1","status":"heuristic","subject":"Root program (node 0)","type":"V"},{"checksum":"0f38e599d64a2e91e7b0ec0b19146e3c4160b86597269d9e6bb179213db32d93","consequence":"the SHAPE of her recipe fits (steps 2-4 analogues); honest label on record: classical theorems in new clothes — the novelty is in the framework/language, not the computations","id":"V2","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"D1-D3 derivations (node 3)","type":"V"},{"checksum":"92aa748246d83af67d9bf0012411ba53a02a8c0c591ae782fbfd6e2202c1dfa4","consequence":"bare limit trivializes: Delta_infinity is the contractible infinite simplex — no topology; the geometry must live in the weights, not the bare complex. OPENED the positivity question — the weights are SIGNED (alternating), not positive.","id":"V3","status":"computationally_verified","subject":"The N->infinity limit (node 4)","type":"V"},{"checksum":"647966a7c47b5aef00dadad5ee7bea2cf45361359bdcf039592d349e5cfb5ad3","consequence":"we have a DICTIONARY (analytic <-> geometric translations), not a bridge. Weil's template: topology supplies the actors, positivity tells them where to stand; our bare complex is contractible — no topology to exploit; the hope lives in the weights, which are signed. The bridge, if it exists, attaches at POSITIVITY — which is node 9. The claim is a research heuristic with precedent, not an established result.","id":"V4","status":"heuristic","subject":"The RH bridge question (node 8)","type":"V"}],"registry":{"B1":"B","B2":"B","B3":"B","C1":"C","C2":"C","D1":"D","D2":"D","D3":"D","D4":"D","D5":"D","D6":"D","D7":"D","D8":"D","G1":"G","G2":"G","G3":"G","L1":"L","L2":"L","V1":"V","V2":"V","V3":"V","V4":"V"},"wire_checksum":"74b4f0aa856bef5f86b72b4f9017175a047fd5d46df515bbfa2c57f2acb815c2"}:TELOMERE-CCC2-1